{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useQueryErrorResetBoundary(): QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx#L102","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx:102"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook will reset any query errors within the closest "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryErrorResetBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":". If there is no boundary\ndefined it will reset them globally."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary'\nimport { useQueryErrorResetBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nfunction App({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const { reset } = useQueryErrorResetBoundary()\n\n  return (\n    <ErrorBoundary\n      onReset={reset}\n      fallbackRender={({ resetErrorBoundary }) => (\n        <div>\n          There was an error!\n          <button onClick={() => resetErrorBoundary()}>Try again</button>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </ErrorBoundary>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useQueryErrorResetBoundary(): QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx:102](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx#L102)\n\nThis hook will reset any query errors within the closest `QueryErrorResetBoundary`. If there is no boundary\ndefined it will reset them globally.\n\n## Returns\n\n`QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue`\n\nThe boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary'\nimport { useQueryErrorResetBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nfunction App({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const { reset } = useQueryErrorResetBoundary()\n\n  return (\n    <ErrorBoundary\n      onReset={reset}\n      fallbackRender={({ resetErrorBoundary }) => (\n        <div>\n          There was an error!\n          <button onClick={() => resetErrorBoundary()}>Try again</button>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </ErrorBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useQueryErrorResetBoundary\ntitle: useQueryErrorResetBoundary\nredirect_from:\n  - framework/react/reference/useQueryErrorResetBoundary\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useQueryErrorResetBoundary(): QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx:102](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx#L102)\n\nThis hook will reset any query errors within the closest `QueryErrorResetBoundary`. If there is no boundary\ndefined it will reset them globally.\n\n## Returns\n\n`QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue`\n\nThe boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary'\nimport { useQueryErrorResetBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nfunction App({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const { reset } = useQueryErrorResetBoundary()\n\n  return (\n    <ErrorBoundary\n      onReset={reset}\n      fallbackRender={({ resetErrorBoundary }) => (\n        <div>\n          There was an error!\n          <button onClick={() => resetErrorBoundary()}>Try again</button>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </ErrorBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
